# annotation-of on a unit constructor with a @[...] annotation (T-1121).
# Unit constructors are a Call expression (not a Fn), so they cannot carry return_ann.
# T-1121 fixes this by wrapping the unit variant in Value::Annotated at eval time:
#   build_constructor_value emits [make-annotated [variant "Tag"] [key: val ...]]
# annotation-of on the resulting Value::Annotated returns the annotation dict directly.
#
# Red@[category: "primary"] → annotation-of Red → Dict({"category": "primary"})
[MyType: [type Red@[category: "primary"]]]
[ann: [annotation-of Red]]
[result: [= [get "category" ann] "primary"]]
=== out
Dict({"result": Bool(true)})

=== warn
unknown parameterized type: Red at 7:16-7:41
undefined variable: Red at 8:22-8:25
